  "threads": [
    {
      "id": "thread-042",
      "title": "Liability frameworks for debris-generating manoeuvres",
      "body": "Who bears responsibility when avoidance manoeuvres fail and generate debris? Current international space law is silent on this — the Outer Space Treaty assigns liability for damage but doesn't address the scenario where a state actor attempts compliance and inadvertently creates a new hazard. I've been drafting a framework that assigns proportional liability based on manoeuvre intent and outcome. Would value input from the Circle before I formalise this as a proposal.",
      "author": "Akello Jane",
      "initials": "AJ",
      "avatar": {},
      "domain": "Space Law",
      "domainColor": "tag-purple",
      "badge": "Endorsed",
