      "pinned": false
    },
    {
      "id": "thread-038",
      "title": "Psychological design in confined habitats",
      "body": "Lessons from Antarctic stations for Mars habitat design. After reviewing 14 months of winterover data from Concordia and Halley VI, I'm seeing consistent patterns in crew psychological deterioration around months 4–6. Key factors: loss of circadian cues, reduced spatial variety, and social fatigue from fixed small-group interaction. These map directly to long-duration transit scenarios. Proposal: can we form a cross-domain working group to translate Antarctic habitability data into Mars transit design constraints?",
      "author": "Namugga Claire",
      "initials": "NC",
      "avatar": { "gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg,var(--amber),#5a3a00)" },
