    {
      "id": "thread-035",
      "title": "Sentinel-2 data access for East Africa",
      "body": "Current limitations and workarounds for remote sensing data access. The Copernicus Open Access Hub is reliable but throughput for East African users is poor — average download times for L2A tiles are 3–5x longer than for European endpoints. I've been testing a mirror setup via Kenya's KEPSA network that cuts this to parity. Sharing my config and benchmark results here. If anyone wants to test the mirror, ping me.",
