    {
      "id": "thread-031",
      "title": "Artemis Accords — East African perspective",
      "body": "The Artemis Accords represent a framework for international cooperation in lunar exploration and beyond. Uganda, as an emerging spacefaring nation, stands to benefit from joining, but there are sovereignty concerns worth discussing. Article 10 on resource extraction could conflict with our existing mineral rights frameworks. However, the cooperation benefits for capacity building are significant. What's the collective view — should we push for an East African consensus position?",
