      "id": "thread-044",
      "title": "End-of-life satellite deorbiting: who pays?",
      "body": "As LEO becomes more congested, the question of who bears the cost of deorbiting defunct satellites is becoming urgent. Current IADC guidelines recommend deorbit within 25 years, but there's no enforcement mechanism and no funding model. I'm working on a proposal for a commons-managed deorbiting fund that would pool contributions from satellite operators proportional to their orbital footprint. Thoughts on the incentive structure?",
      "author": "Mensah Nii",
